# Run: dotnet run --project samples/Shop.MinimalApi
@host = http://localhost:5180
@orderId = paste-an-order-id-here

### Customer error codes (orders_, payments_)
GET {{host}}/api/error-codes

### Admin error codes (also admin_): 401 without a user, 403 for a customer
GET {{host}}/api/admin/error-codes
X-User: root
X-Role: admin

### 401 from the auth gate, same body as every other error
POST {{host}}/api/orders

### Create an order
POST {{host}}/api/orders
X-User: alice
X-Role: customer

### 422 Invalid: validation errors keyed like the JSON
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/lines
X-User: alice
X-Role: customer
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "", "quantity": 9 }

### 400 orders_1002: not enough stock (TEE has 3)
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/lines
X-User: alice
X-Role: customer
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "TEE", "quantity": 4 }

### 200: add a line
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/lines
X-User: alice
X-Role: customer
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "MUG", "quantity": 2 }

### 403 orders_1003: someone else's order
GET {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
X-User: bob
X-Role: customer

### Admin: take the payment provider down
PUT {{host}}/api/admin/payment-provider
X-User: root
X-Role: admin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "is_down": true }

### 503 payments_1001: provider down (a 4th attempt within a minute is 429 rate_limited)
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/pay
X-User: alice
X-Role: customer

### 409 admin_1001: refund an unpaid order
POST {{host}}/api/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/refund
X-User: root
X-Role: admin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 5 }
